  "summary_text": "Kyle, Friday delivered mixed signals across both stores, but the month-to-date picture is unambiguously strong and calendar-adjusted performance at Hicksville is exceptional.\n\nPort Washington came in soft yesterday\u2014down 12% total revenue\u2014but this is a capacity story, not a performance story. You ran 4 groomers producing $398 per groomer-day versus a trailing 30-day baseline of $469; that $71 gap explains the dip. The concerning piece: retail collapsed 71% ($143 vs $492), suggesting either inventory friction or front-of-house focus slipped. Core groom revenue actually held up (+3%), and add-on attach improved to 50% (up from 44%), so your team's upsell discipline is solid. Month-to-date, Port is tracking +8% ($87,961 vs DOW-adjusted expectation of $86,126), and year-to-date you're up 44% on appointments\u2014that's the real story. Retail reorder list is live (Shanti's Medical Journey, bully sticks, treat tables); prioritize replenishment.\n\nHicksville is running hot. Yesterday's 20% revenue jump came on 5 groomer-days at $346 per groomer\u2014below baseline, but the month speaks louder: +26% actual vs +18.8% DOW-adjusted, meaning real operational lift. Add-on revenue dropped sharply to $55 (from $115), signaling an upsell discipline opportunity worth coaching. You have zero bather hours scheduled for the next 7 days at Hicksville; that's a structural constraint worth examining if demand is there. Hicksville's lapse pool is smaller than Port's ($91k vs $297k annual value), but the 53 drifting customers suggest visit-cadence stretch\u2014worth a reactivation campaign.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Port has 4 groomer-days + 8h bathers today, 1 groomer + 15h bathers tomorrow; Hicksville has 3 groomer-days + 0h bathers today, 0 groomer-days tomorrow; next 7 days scheduled 35 groomer-days at Port and 18 at Hicksville.**"
